Fast terminal with native tabs, splits and GPU-accelerated rendering

Ghostty is a terminal emulator that aims to be fast, feature-rich and native at the same time. It renders with the GPU on its own threads, uses a GTK interface on Linux, and runs every mainstream terminal program without issue. This is an unofficial AppImage build of Ghostty that runs on any Linux distribution.

- Multiple windows, tabs and split panes, with tab renaming and coloring
- GPU rendering with OpenGL and a multi-threaded design for low latency
- Broad support for modern escape sequences, including the Kitty graphics protocol
- Hundreds of built-in color themes with light and dark mode switching
- Plain-text configuration with sensible defaults
